
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:resize@

%9Description:%9

    Checks the size of the terminal again and, if the number of columns or
    lines changed, resizes the windows and redraws the screen. If the size
    did not change, nothing happens; use REDRAW to redraw the screen anyway.

    This is normally done automatically when erssi receives the window
    size change signal (SIGWINCH); the command helps when that signal was
    missed.

%9Examples:%9

    /RESIZE

%9See also:%9 REDRAW, WINDOW

